From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: PCI: qcom: reject short SID maps and invalid provider widths

A nonempty IOMMU map can contain too few cells for a complete entry.
Reject it before looking up its provider. Reject zero or excessive
specifier widths before computing the entry stride. The four-cell
legacy format for a two-cell provider remains valid.

Fixes: 5121d76cb9dd ("PCI: qcom: Honor IOMMU provider's #iommu-cells in qcom_pcie_config_sid_1_9_0()")
Link: https://github.com/slwyts/Project-SunUEFI/commit/e8fcf33971263f28085dbc0dbe5039438bf76c13
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
index 95850f91c91b0d42dec1f33ca8f0db7f3690cec7..1f17d07c09b92f94ae997779f0caa928942f8b8c 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -1317,7 +1317,7 @@ static int qcom_pcie_config_sid_1_9_0(struct qcom_pcie *pcie)
 	if (!map || !size)
 		return 0;
 
-	if (size % sizeof(*map)) {
+	if (size < 4 * sizeof(*map) || size % sizeof(*map)) {
 		dev_err(dev, "Malformed iommu-map property\n");
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
@@ -1340,6 +1340,11 @@ static int qcom_pcie_config_sid_1_9_0(struct qcom_pcie *pcie)
 		iommu_cells = 1;
 	of_node_put(iommu_np);
 
+	/* A four-cell legacy entry can reference a two-cell provider. */
+	if (!iommu_cells || iommu_cells > nr_cells - 2) {
+		dev_err(dev, "Invalid IOMMU specifier width in iommu-map\n");
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
 	entry_cells = 3 + iommu_cells;
 
 	/*
